AB  - The US Department of Defense is investing in a variety of next-generation technologies, including weapon systems, improved sensors and modeling technologies, to help improve the capabilities of US forces in urban warfare. The Defense Advanced Research Projects Agency (DARPA) has granted several awards for projects on cultured training and computer modeling of urban combat and post-conflict situations. The projects include a robot armed with an electronic gun that could fire either non-lethal or lethal grounds. DARPA also granted awards on projects on advanced sensors to better detect explosives and individuals and carry out persistent surveillance.
