TI  - Urban warfare equipment put to the test in UK
PY  - 2005
T2  - Jane's Defence Weekly
IS  - MAY
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84860980127?origin=resultslist
AB  - British combat units were exposed to 'transformational' urban warfare equipment during a three-week experimental exercise earlier in year 2005. 'Urban Exercise 2' (URBEX 2) involved futuristic weapon systems and survelliance sensors being put through their paces by British soldiers and Royal Marines under the watchful eye of experts from the Defence Procurement Agency (DPA) and Ministry of Defence Equipment Capability organization. The exercise in February 2005 was the second of a series where commercial off-the-shelf products were hired or borrowed to be assessed in realistic conditions at the British Army's purpose-built urban warfare training center at Wiltshire. Technology is the urban warfare sphere moves forward at a rapid pace.
